"""
Pseudonyms of personal data, a client address for one, for what is kept
and logged: the HMAC-SHA256 of the value under a key of the
server, in hex.  The same value gives the same pseudonym as long as the
key stays, so a pseudonym can be counted and compared, and without the key
it cannot be turned back.

There is no pseudonym without a key: a plain SHA-256 of an IPv4 address
is turned back by trying all 2^32 of them.  The key is a machine key of
at least 32 bytes (Wolly.Secret); the HMAC is taken under the HMAC of the
purpose under it, so the key of the pseudonyms is not the key of anything
else even when one file serves two purposes.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);

module Wolly.Pseudonym is
    """
    The hex digits of a pseudonym: 64.
    """
    function pseudonymDigits(): Index
        ensures result = 64;

    """
    The pseudonym of value under key.  None when key is shorter than 32
    bytes or libcrypto fails.
    No contract: a short key is answered with None, not refused, and the
    digest is the work of libcrypto.
    """
    generic [K: Region, V: Region]
    function pseudonym(key: Span[Nat8, K], value: Span[Nat8, V]): Option[String];
end module.
